# Pseudoautosomal regions of CHM13 chrX, where a male sample carries two copies.
#
# Not looked up: read off the T2T-Q100 truth itself, which is diploid at 11,683 chrX records in
# exactly two blocks and haploid at 120,704. Everything outside these intervals keeps the ploidy
# given by -d.
#
# CHROM must match the contig as the output VCF spells it (chrX), not the graph path name
# (CHM13#0#chrX).
chrX	0	2394370	2
chrX	153926003	154259566	2
